{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested at exact head 946a52eaf8e056f648f796a796a1e3cab750d006, resting on all 69 submitted artifacts, packages/client/README.md first. Review f7c79158 is partly addressed: the two original different-lane reproductions now pass, recovery uses the recorded workspace path instead of the retry command's directory, and a different newer landing is preserved. Sixty artifacts are byte-identical to revision 3; all nine changed files were reviewed in full. The four added lockfile descriptors exactly match the approved lane L revision 4 metadata.\n\nP2 — Fence local recovery by version and lease identity, not lane ID alone (packages/cli/src/main.ts applyLocal, especially lines 279 and 295–305; packages/cli/src/git.ts credentialLane/removeCredential, lines 60–74; config.ts LocalIntent/workspaces). Independent diagnostics reproduce two remaining forms of the same ownership issue:\n1. Claim lane X and install its lease-1 workspace. Release with a stable idempotency key, interrupted at act-answered. Reclaim X and install its lease-2 workspace. Retry the old release. The credential marker explicitly says lease 2, but credentialLane discards that number and removeCredential matches only X. Recovery deletes the newer credential, removes the selected X and deletes its current workspace mapping. There is exactly one remote release; the new lease is still active.\n2. Select X, start a claim for Y interrupted at act-answered (saved expect is X), finish a newer claim for Z, then deliberately choose X again with claim --lane X. Recover the old Y claim. Because the selected ID once again equals expect, recovery silently changes the selected lane to Y. Equality of a value does not prove that no newer local action happened.\nPersist the released lease and workspace installation ownership with the prepared journal, and compare it against the current credential/config ownership before cleanup. Preserve newer ownership of the same lane, not only a different lane. Give lane selection and other mutable local selections a revision or owner token that records intervening local actions, including a selection that returns to its earlier ID; use that in repeat-safe completion. Keep signed receipt recovery independent of fresh sessions or authority, and report skipped historical side effects clearly. Add both reproductions with interrupted writes and repeat recovery, alongside the now-passing different-lane/other-directory cases. Do not infer current lease ownership by reissuing the remote act.\n\nArchitecture: centralizing LocalIntent and applyLocal is a useful step, and the prepared/answered receipt protocol remains sound. The ownership fence is still incomplete because a lane persists across leases and local values can recur. The full E client/CLI/MCP scope and amendment 2 remain required.\nSecurity: credential redaction, room-ID checks, authority-first bearer replay, retained signed receipts, MCP own-property dispatch and stream error/cancellation behavior remain intact. An old local release must not remove authorization material for a later lease. The diagnostic uses a fake Room and real local Git/config files, not a live service.\nSimplification: retain the shared local completion function. A durable revision/ownership token gives one precise rule for fresh and recovered commands, rather than additional lane-value exceptions. The binary-only CLI package remains correctly packaged.\n\nValidation: isolated clean install of 340 packages; root strict typecheck passed. All 86 client Node and 2 client workerd, 50 CLI, 66 MCP Node and 1 MCP workerd tests passed. CLI build (940.6 KiB), bundled help and four-file dry package passed. Two independent diagnostics pin the remaining same-lane/new-lease and reselected-lane defects. The existing review tests verify the different-lane and other-directory repairs. No builder source was edited and no deployment, live token creation or remote repository mutation was performed. Schedule estimates do not reduce functionality.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:45343d488677fc827ddf9ca5307641705b4096e4","binding":"assigned","head":"946a52eaf8e056f648f796a796a1e3cab750d006","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:510f65a9552ec727f41d513e78e1448cfd308ad2\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:3f934a98fa8efcc34c1695fee9b59e58568876e3\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6c466548c785a19fd57fd8bd104701c37d2b58af","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}